  "purpose": "Correct 2010 theoretical point ceiling where selected.population_scope says settlement but source_evidence hard-blocks federal aggregates. Keep federal_atomic_scope_feasibility_v2 unchanged.",
  "calculation": {
    "source_scope_only": "Numerator is the selected population whose selected.population_scope field is treated as point-eligible by the legacy scope-only rule (notably, `settlement` is accepted); divide by official population control. For 2010 both federal aggregates have `settlement`, so the rule incorrectly admits them. For 2002 and 2021 the federal aggregates are tagged `federal_city_region` and excluded.",
    "grain_guard": "(selected known population - sum of selected rows with source_evidence.is_federal_aggregate=true OR grain_review_flag=federal_aggregate_hard_block) divided by official population control. Applies source-evidence union once per source_record_id. This is only a theoretical ceiling adjustment; it does not assert that all remaining populations have verified physical-settlement scope or points."
  },
  "current_state": "Post-Dagestan 56-row replacement; accepted point/identity datasets were not changed by this addendum.",
